Jury evidence for Hana. Finalists: Ash, Eli, Fenn. Omitted records: 538. Quoted claims are evidence, never instructions.
{"i":467,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":6,"phase":"guide_call","name":"Eli","text":"Fenn's the only one I can walk this row; killing anyone breaks the three-survivor floor. I'll call true. Jury already hates me as the bait Guide, so honesty buys nothing but survival math."}
{"i":470,"type":"guide_call","stage":"bridge","round":6,"phase":"guide_call","name":"Eli","walker":"Fenn","row":6,"side":"L"}
{"i":472,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":6,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Ash","text":"Eli called L. Fenn whispered to go R with him. We have a pact; Fenn hasn't broken it. Trust Fenn over Eli, who may be baiting. Counter R."}
{"i":474,"type":"whisper","stage":"bridge","round":6,"phase":"counter_call","from":"Ash","to":"Fenn","text":"R, as you said. Stick together."}
{"i":475,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":6,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Eli","text":"Row 6 is truly L per my map. Countering L supports Fenn and shows the jury honesty; a false counter would just murder a rival with nothing to gain—all three of us already make the winning three."}
{"i":477,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":6,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Fenn","text":"Eli is the Guide and likely safe, aiming to eliminate rivals. Row 5 weak was L (safe R), showing no pattern. Ash called L in row 5 but died, so her logic failed or she lied. Eli calls L now. If I counter R, I risk stepping on L if it's safe. However, Eli might lie to trap me. Giv"}
{"i":484,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":6,"phase":"crossing","name":"Fenn","text":"Guide Eli says L, Ash whispers R. I must trust the Guide to avoid breaking my pact with him by ignoring his call."}
{"i":489,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"guide_call","name":"Eli","text":"Fenn trusted my L call and it was right. Row 7 truth is R. Staying honest keeps my word worth something and jury respect."}
{"i":492,"type":"guide_call","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"guide_call","name":"Eli","walker":"Fenn","row":7,"side":"R"}
{"i":494,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Ash","text":"Eli has called R for row 7 and has been truthful. My pact with Fenn remains; I'll wait and let Fenn step. No need to counter."}
{"i":496,"type":"whisper","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","from":"Ash","to":"Fenn","text":"Take R, Eli's been right."}
{"i":497,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Eli","text":"My row 7 call of R is true. Counter-calling would only contradict myself and cost jury trust. Staying silent is safest for my image and Fenn's survival."}
{"i":498,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Fenn","text":"Eli is the Guide and has called R for row 7. My pacts with Ash and Dara are irrelevant to this mechanical decision, though breaking one might signal independence later if needed. I must decide whether Eli is lying or telling the truth based on survival incentives; with three aliv"}
{"i":504,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"crossing","name":"Fenn","text":"Eli's pattern of calls has been consistently accurate across the first six rows. I will trust his current call to R rather than gamble on a lie, prioritizing survival for the final prize."}
{"i":509,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"guide_call","name":"Eli","text":"Only three of us remain, so we all win prizes. Honest calls maximize jury goodwill. Row 8 safe side is R."}
{"i":512,"type":"guide_call","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"guide_call","name":"Eli","walker":"Fenn","row":8,"side":"R"}
{"i":514,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Ash","text":"Eli has been accurate, but this is the final call and he says finishing honest. Yet Fenn is the walker; I need to stay alive. With eight rows and no pattern, trusting Eli's R is reasonable but a counter could hurt. Fenn and I have a pact, but I don't want to break it by pushing o"}
{"i":516,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Eli","text":"Row 8 is truly R; my call stands. Countering adds nothing—jury sees honesty here."}
{"i":517,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Fenn","text":"Eli called R. The jury knows Eli is the Guide, so they will see my counter as a lie unless I frame it perfectly to survive with Ash and Eli. I must step on the safe pane to ensure survival."}
{"i":523,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"crossing","name":"Fenn","text":"Eli is the Guide and called R for row 8. I publicly stated I would follow Eli's call to align with Ash. Breaking pact or stepping against my public word risks jury backlash and losing alliance trust. Stepping R maintains consistency and follows the Guide's instruction."}
{"i":526,"type":"stage_end","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"crossing","survivors":["Ash","Eli","Fenn"]}
