{"i":564,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Ash","text":"Eli tried to accept Fenn's offer but failed, and Fenn broke pact with me. I still have a pact with Eli, but Fenn is risky. I can't break Eli yet; maybe keep the pact for safety or offer Fenn to bind him? Jury might judge if I break Eli. Better to wait and observe; no need to act "}
{"i":565,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Eli","text":"Fenn's warning may be bait to split me from Ash. Keeping Ash and also locking Fenn covers both paths; no betrayal costs."}
{"i":567,"type":"whisper","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","from":"Eli","to":"Fenn","text":"If Ash truly turns, tell me at the lever, not before."}
{"i":568,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Fenn","text":"Ash and Eli are aligned against me. I must break their pact to survive the final hazard stage. Offering a pact to Ash creates a wedge and potentially breaks his alliance with Eli, though breaking my existing pact with Dara was necessary to isolate myself from past alliances."}
