{"i":612,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","name":"Eli","text":"Final three locked. Breaking a pact now only angers the jury and invites retaliation. Keep both pacts intact and see how the next hazard plays out."}
{"i":613,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","name":"Fenn","text":"All three are finalists with no vote possible. Jury sees pacts; breaking Eli's makes me look ruthless but could signal independence to the jury who may value autonomy over alliances."}
{"i":619,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Ash","text":"We have three alive and pacts with Eli and Eli-Fenn. I need to read the jury. Bex and Dara had pact, but both eliminated; that might matter. My pact with Eli is intact; Fenn has pacts with both of us, a potential swing. I'll keep Eli close but maybe plant doubt about Fenn's loyal"}
{"i":621,"type":"whisper","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","from":"Ash","to":"Eli","text":"Fenn pacts with both of us. Watch him."}
{"i":622,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Eli","text":"Final three already secured; pacts are dormant but breaking them now only angers the jury. Wait and save my words for the endgame."}
{"i":623,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","name":"Fenn","text":"I have pacts with both Eli and Ash. The hazard is imminent; keeping all three alive maximizes my survival odds against the jury. Breaking a pact now signals treachery and reduces my alliance support."}
{"i":625,"type":"whisper","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","from":"Fenn","to":"Eli","text":"Stay close. If Ash falters, we decide together."}
{"i":629,"type":"stage_end","stage":"pacts","round":2,"phase":"pacts","survivors":["Ash","Eli","Fenn"]}
